{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Elohim, hasten</b> — because of <b>אלהים</b> at the beginning, as though it were written: \"Elohim, hasten to deliver me,\" in the manner of (Proverbs 20:27) <b>נר אלהים נשמת אדם</b> (\"the lamp of YHWH is the soul of man\"), and many are like this."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 70, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:46.129844406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}